### Step 6 — Search, filters and sorting (public, no login). VS Code "REST Client".
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Filter choices + slider ranges for the browse page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/meta/filters

### Everything, trending first (default sort POPULAR)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?size=5

### Keyword (title, description, ingredient; stemmed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?q=chickpea

### Vegetarian eater → Veg + Vegan + Jain recipes (from the Recipe class hierarchy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?diet=VEG&size=50

### Regionality + food type
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?cuisine=PAN_ASIAN,THAI&course=MAIN,APPETIZER

### What can I cook with only these? (salt, oil, spices assumed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?ingredients=cooked rice,lemon,peanuts,green chilli&ingredientMatch=ONLY

### Must use both tomato and garlic
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?ingredients=tomato,garlic

### Only the utensils I have
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?equipment=blender

### Budget, time, nutrition, difficulty, rating — cheapest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?maxCost=150&maxMinutes=30&maxCalories=400&minProtein=5&maxDifficulty=2&minRating=4&sort=CHEAPEST

### Invalid parameter → 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?maxDifficulty=9
